														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4270462">
									

<p>You were actually spot on with most of these! This SCP is the second entry in my <a href="/literallymechanical-s-author-page">Pennsylvania Dark</a> series, about a secretive cult in rural Pennsylvania called the Nachtkarich &#8212; but they're not a doomsday cult. They have access to some rudimentary occult techniques, mostly around long-distance telepathy and information transfer, but their primary weapons are lots and lots of guns and home-made pipe bombs. They're fanatics, ready to fight to the deaths of every man, woman, and child in their village against the evils of the Foundation/United States government/any authority figure whom their leader tells them to hate.</p>
<p>They're aware of the Foundation, and allowed the Instruction Manual (of which this is, indeed, the only copy) to fall into the Foundation's hands. They're using it as a kind of psychological warfare, sending the Foundation on a wild goose chase after fictional copies of an instruction manual for a fictional dark god.</p>
<p>The kill count is made up, as well, and is an attempt to make the Foundation fearful and uncertain. The only thing that was real is that they hacked a Foundation computer terminal, and killed a Foundation employee in a drive-by shooting.</p>
<p>I'm curious to know what plot thread you were imagining?</p>

